  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p> Your opponent plunges his weapon deep into your chest. You suffer what is called a tension pneumothorax, meaning your lung collapses as air enters the pleural space between lung and chest wall, each breath you try to take causing further air to enter but not get out as the edges of the wound act as a valve. As air builds up it starts obstructing the workings of the other lung and heart.</p> <p><strong>Effects:</strong> You gain @Condition[Fatigued] (1), gaining another level at the end of each of your subsequent turns. When you have reached @Condition[Fatigued] (10) you expire. This accumulation can only be stopped using Surgery. If successful Surgery is applied your @Condition[Fatigued] Condition is immediately reduced to @Condition[Fatigued] (3). For healing purposes, count as Torn Muscle (Major) with partial healing reducing your Condition from @Condition[Fatigued] (3) to @Condition[Fatigued] (1) which will be removed once fully healed.</p>"
    },
